{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/96519-how-are-season-kings-and-queens-picked","id":96519,"title":"How are Season Kings and Queens picked?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-22T13:51:50-07:00","id":96519,"title":"How are Season Kings and Queens picked?","content":"Already asked on rpg.net but I might also see what thoughts people have here... the books are pretty vague on the topic, which process are used to pick Kings &amp; Queens of the Courts, and how much of it is mundane, how much is magical?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2314-salinea","name":"salinea","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T13:57:30-07:00","id":96520,"title":"","content":"It's a flexible affair. It can be that the current king or queen pick someone to suceed them, they're picked by the elders or office holders of a court, popular vote, contests appropriate to the court, etc. It's one of those things that changes from freehold to freehold, based on the laws and pledges used in the foundation and adjustment of each court in an area.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T05:10:40-07:00","id":98279,"title":"","content":"I have the crowns appear on the head of one of the courts each appropiate season. In other words, they are picked by the season itself. I am sure I took this from a book that said either this or something that I thought was this <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2585-alejandro","name":"Alejandro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T15:36:15-07:00","id":98714,"title":"","content":"A few of the books have Miami-based stories that mention the crowns. The impression I got from those is that the crowns start to manifest when a particular Court leader begins to make clear their intent to take power. So while Naamah professes loyalty to Grandfather Thunder, her crown is almost non-existent. But then in... Swords at Dawn, I think, it's mentioned that her crown is growing more clearly defined as Autumn begins to gear up towards opposing Summer openly.<br /> <br /> Or something along those lines.<br /> <br /> As ArcaneArts mentioned, the process can be whatever system seems most appropriate for your Freehold. It could be anything from the current leader of a court naming their successor, to democratic elections.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T19:44:41-07:00","id":98883,"title":"","content":"The books aren't entirely clear on this. It seems to be in part a matter of charisma and personal power, but Lords of Summer gives a few more detailed methods. The King of Summer is the person people think of as being the leader, though if you knock that guy's head off you get the crown. I think Spring is essentially a popularity contest. Autumn and Winter are to the best of my knowledge unspecified, but given their natures knowledge of the occult and degree of initiation into Winter's mystery cult seem like the obvious choices. Really though the simplest option is that the person with the highest mantle gets the crown unless something else comes up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1266-sirpants","name":"SirPants","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T20:34:53-07:00","id":99694,"title":"","content":"In my game, it's generally whichever individual most exemplifies their court. Summer is the finest soldier, Spring is whoever desires the crown the most, Autumn is the greatest occultist, and Winter... Winter is funny, because it's so small that the members all live together in the one house. The King/Queen is probably just whoever feels most comfortable taking the crown.<br /> <br /> I have a friend who is running a game where the Freehold has two leaders per Season, one King and one Queen. As a rule, when one ruling member moves on, the remaining one picks a successor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T00:13:46-07:00","id":99807,"title":"","content":"I love e idea of a King and a Queen <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> sounds like a lot of interesting stuff can be done there <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2585-alejandro","name":"Alejandro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T10:05:12-07:00","id":100128,"title":"","content":"In a past game ...<br /> <br /> The Summer Monarch of the freehold was the victor of the annual Summer Games, which is a week long competition which culminates with the crowning of the victor on the Summer Solstice. The games are bloody and harsh, testing both the mettle and the conviction of its participants.<br /> <br /> The King/Queen of Autumn is the keeper of the Balefire, which is a fiery fairy spirit that can only be caught and bound by a skilled magician. The spirit is capricious and mercurial. It constantly struggles against its bondage and when it finds a weakness in the magics that keeps it imprisoned, it escapes and takes the Autumn Crown with it.<br /> <br /> The Winter Crown is coveted by every hobgoblin and fairy creature that dwells within the Hedge. The Monarch of the Season has a responsibility to keep it, and thus himself, completely hidden from all that wish to possess it. No outsider (barring those with high Court Goodwill) has met or even seen the current Winter King. If the identity of the Monarch is ever revealed, the Crown is relinquished to a courtier that has a better chance at keeping it hidden.<br /> <br /> The Spring Court's ruler is determined by beauty, either personal or by possession. Each courtier strives to possess the most desirable aspect of beauty, and during the &quot;off season&quot; they compete with each other by hosting and attending sumptuous parties, gallery exhibitions and performances. Personal attractiveness and style is only one small arena in which one could compete. More sought after is the cultivation and the creation of beautiful things and experiences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","user":"Firefly Night","date":". 03-27-2014, 05:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}